# Write gate

`AGENTS.md` § *Write gate* is the full statement of these rules and governs; this
file exists so they are in context from the first message of every session. When
the two disagree, `AGENTS.md` wins.

**Analysis is the default.** "Review", "check", "look at", "see if", "is there
anything wrong with" are requests for a report, not for changes. Report what you
find and stop. Do not apply fixes, not even obvious or trivial ones.

**Editing needs the exact phrase.** Only edit when the user has sent, verbatim:
"For the love of everything, please edit, please help me". Ambiguous wording
("fix it", "sort this out", "can you handle it") is not approval — ask which
files you may touch before writing anything. Approval covers only the change
described. It does not extend to the next file, the next finding, or the next
turn.

**One standing exception.** Notes under `docs/knowledge/` may be created and
edited without the phrase, but only as the `knowledge-note` skill — the rules in
`.agents/skills/knowledge-note/SKILL.md`, which you must read and follow before
writing a note. Cursor has no skill mechanism, so declare it explicitly by
running `npm run gate:note` first. Deleting a note is never covered.

**Once approved.** Re-read every file immediately before writing to it; the
author edits these files too, sometimes mid-session. Make only the approved
change, and mention anything else you notice rather than fixing it. Leave the
result uncommitted — the author commits, and does not want an agent co-author
trailer. Never run `git checkout`, `git restore`, `git reset`, `git clean`, or
`git stash` to discard working-tree changes.

**Sources and citations.** Every factual claim carries the URL actually fetched,
plus the work's title and identifier. A source that could not be fetched is
reported as unfetched, in those words, never cited from memory. Anything worked
out rather than read is marked as inferred, in that word. Every path, filename,
flag and command carries its `file:line`.

## This is enforced, not merely asked

`.cursor/hooks.json` runs `tools/write-gate/gate.mjs` on every prompt, every
tool call, and every shell command. It gates one thing: changing this
repository's content. Edits inside the repo outside `docs/knowledge/` are denied
without approval, note writes are denied when the skill is not open, `git add`,
`commit` and `push` are denied because the author does those personally, and
`git checkout`, `restore`, `reset`, `clean` and `stash` are denied outright.

Everything else runs normally — `gh` and the issue tracker, `npm install`, test
runs, dev servers, `node`, `python`, and any write whose target is outside the
repository. See `AGENTS.md` § *The gate is enforced, not merely asked* for the
full list.

Do not attempt to work around it: not by asking the user to disable the hook,
not through a shell redirect, and not through an interpreter. If the gate blocks
something the user genuinely wants, say so and ask them for the phrase.
